      "text": [
        "586 - وَقَالَ أَبُو جَعْفَرٍ اَلْبَاقِرُ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ: «غُسْلُ اَلْمَيِّتِ مِثْلُ غُسْلِ اَلْجُنُبِ فَإِنْ كَانَ كَثِيرَ اَلشَّعْرِ فَرُدَّ اَلْمَاءَ عَلَيْهِ ثَلاَثَ مَرَّاتٍ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.586 - Imam Muhammad ibn Ali Al-Baqir (as) said:\n\"The washing (ghusl) of the deceased is like the washing of one in a state of major ritual impurity (ghusl al-janabah). If the deceased has a lot of hair, then pour water over it three times.\""
        ]
      }
